body:
The new "pipeline" kanban view uses a spec-style `kanban.groupByField`, but the console/list rendering code expects kanban grouping under `options.kanban.groupField` (or a flattened `groupBy/groupField`). As-is, the Pipeline view will likely default to grouping by "status" instead of "stage". Consider either adding the expected `options.kanban.groupField` alongside the existing config, or updating the console view->options mapping to translate `kanban.groupByField` to `options.kanban.groupField`.
```suggestion
          },
          options: {
            kanban: {
              groupField: 'stage',
            },
          },
```

The new "calendar" view defines its fields under `calendar.startDateField/endDateField/titleField`, but the console view rendering path currently reads flattened `startDateField/endDateField/titleField` (or `options.calendar.*`). Without normalization, this will fall back to defaults (e.g., due_date/start_date) and may render an empty/broken calendar for `event`. Consider adding `options.calendar.{startDateField,endDateField,titleField}` (or updating the mapping code to use `viewDef.calendar.*`).
```suggestion
          },
          options: {
            calendar: {
              startDateField: 'start',
              endDateField: 'end',
              titleField: 'subject',
            },
          },
```
